# HRM screens (Workdo parity)

When building or updating HRM admin UI (`apps/web` HRM routes/components/mock data):

## Structure (AgainERP, not Workdo chrome)

- Reuse existing AgainERP patterns: `HrmEntityPage` / dedicated pages like employees & attendance records, ghost icon row actions (`Button variant="ghost" size="icon" className="h-7 w-7 rounded-none"`), resizable `Sheet` for view/edit, square UI (`rounded-none`).
- Do **not** invent colored solid action pills, circular avatars, or Workdo-only chrome that fights ERP UI rules.
- Prefer copying an existing dedicated HRM page (employees, attendance records, timesheet) over a new visual system.

## Fields & data (Workdo demo)

- Field sets, statuses, filters, and seed content come from Workdo HRM demo / user manual (e.g. [demo.workdo.io/hrm](https://demo.workdo.io/hrm/), Workdo HRM docs).
- Match demo columns/actions/workflows with **mock data**; keep real API for later.

## Search (always realtime)

- Table/list **Search** filters the current dataset **as the user types** (bind filter to the input value; do not require clicking Search).
- Keep a Search button only for Workdo chrome parity if needed; it must not be required for filtering.
- On change: update search state + reset page to 1.

## After UI/seed changes — clear cache so the user sees output instantly

Always run before telling the user to check:

```powershell
docker compose stop web
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force apps/web/.next -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
docker compose up -d --no-deps --force-recreate web
```

Then remind: **Ctrl+Shift+R** on the page.
